Checkpoint 5 validation runbook - Windy image acquisition
==========================================================

Checkpoint outcome to validate
------------------------------

Checkpoint 5 must retrieve due active Windy streams, refresh provider image
metadata, skip unchanged markers, download and fully validate changed preview
images, and update ingestion state at the correct stages. It must not upload
to S3 or publish MQTT notifications.

This runbook is prepared in advance. Commands and expected outputs must be
updated to match the implemented command-line interface before checkpoint 5
is submitted for acceptance.

1. Confirm branch and protected configuration
---------------------------------------------

    cd /home/codexuser/src/webcam-iot-ingest
    git branch --show-current
    git status --short
    git diff --check
    git check-ignore -v .env .secrets/windy_api_key .secrets/database_password

The branch must be codex. Do not print secret values or discard unrelated
working-tree changes.

2. Start and verify PostgreSQL
------------------------------

    docker compose --env-file .env up -d postgres
    docker compose exec postgres pg_isready
    uv run --env-file .env python -m database.healthcheck

Do not delete or recreate the PostgreSQL volume.

3. Run focused automated tests
------------------------------

    uv run --env-file .env pytest tests/ingestion/windy -v
    RUN_DATABASE_TESTS=1 uv run --env-file .env pytest tests/database/test_registry_queries.py -v
    uv run --env-file .env python -m ingestion.windy.windy_ingestion_workflow --help

Tests must cover unchanged markers, valid changed images, invalid or oversized
bodies, missing webcams and renditions, expired URLs, throttling, bounded
retries, and database state transitions.

4. Run bounded dry-run and acquisition checks
---------------------------------------------

    uv run --env-file .env python -m ingestion.windy.windy_ingestion_workflow --once --dry-run --limit 5
    uv run --env-file .env python -m ingestion.windy.windy_ingestion_workflow --once --limit 5

The dry run must not update PostgreSQL. The applied run must not print
tokenized image URLs or credentials and must not contact S3 or MQTT.

5. Inspect and repeat state transitions
---------------------------------------

    docker compose exec postgres psql -U webcam_ingestion -d webcam_ingestion -c \
      "SELECT source_stream_id, status, last_provider_image_marker, last_download_timestamp, ema_download_period FROM source_stream ss JOIN site s USING (site_id) WHERE s.network_id = 'win' ORDER BY last_download_timestamp DESC NULLS LAST LIMIT 20;"
    uv run --env-file .env python -m ingestion.windy.windy_ingestion_workflow --once --limit 5

Confirm successful downloads update marker, timestamp, and EMA; unchanged
markers skip image bodies and do not advance the successful timestamp; failed
requests do not claim success; and inactive or blacklisted streams are not
queried.

6. Final review and decision
----------------------------

    git diff --check
    git status --short
    git diff

Checkpoint 5 is accepted only after focused tests, bounded live acquisition,
unchanged-marker behavior, database state transitions, and secret review pass.
Stop before checkpoint 6.
